Subject: The compiled constructor cache is keyed on shape_free_epoch too, and refuses an answer once the prototype watchpoint has saturated

What this does
  - `JSAotCtorCache` gains `sfe`, the value of `rt->shape_free_epoch` when the answer was filled. `qjs_aot_ctor_replayable`'s fast path and the generated twin of it (the vweb construct arm in ops.c) both compare it.
  - `shape_free_epoch` moves from the tail of `JSRuntime` to next to `aot_pic_epoch`, and its offset is exported (`off_rt_shape_free_epoch`, `QJS_AOT_OFF_RT_SHAPE_FREE_EPOCH`) so a unit can read it. Where it was, its offset followed a block of optional fields and differed between the generator's engine build and the runtime's.
  - `qjs_aot_ctor_replayable` returns 0 once `ic_watchpoint_epoch` has reached `JS_IC_EPOCH_MAX`.

Why we need it
  The cache remembers `ctor->shape` as a raw address and, on a hit, reads `ctor->prop[cc->slot]` against it. A shape that is freed and reallocated at the same address with different contents (the constructor
  function object's own shape changing, its old shape freed, a new one allocated there) matched, and `slot` then indexed a shape it was not computed for. Nothing compared `shape_free_epoch`, which exists for exactly this.
  Past saturation `ic_watchpoint_epoch` stops moving, so the cells' equality test against it can no longer detect a prototype interceptor; no cell is filled then (0421), but the answer is also refused here.

Cost
  One load and one branch on a hit. Measured with the compare in place: raytrace 1282.8 -> 1282.8 C.Minstr, deltablue 790.5 -> 790.5, so the frees that move the epoch do not reach the cache's steady state.
  (If a kernel ever loses more than 1% here, compare against the counted `cb->ctor_fn_shape` in the slow path instead: a shape the bytecode holds a reference to cannot be recycled.)

Soundness
  Fill and hit see the same `shape_free_epoch` only if no shape was freed or edited in place in between (0420 moves it for in-place edits), so a recycled address is never taken for the shape recorded.
  `.local/kit/cases/stub_sat.js` forces saturation (9000 interceptor events on prototypes) and checks that constructors and stores, cached before and first run after saturation, still honour a setter added afterwards.

Functions touched
  `qjs_aot_ctor_replayable`, `js_aot_gen_layout`, `JSRuntime` (field moved), `JSAotCtorCache`, `JSAotGenLayout`.

No.

